text:
Where is it summer and where winter ?
I am not there yet, but I shall be;
And so you must bear your burden meekly ;
But wait until I return with treasure.

We've met, we're friends together,
And with my arms I clasp thy neck;

There is no grief or fear for me,
Nor any care nor pain to seek;

The moon was full, and she shone on me

And her pale light stole o'er my soul;

I saw, I heard - but it was only thee!

Acrostic Poem for <b>MOM</b>
(M)other and (O)ne with whom I have grown up;
(A)lways ready to take care of us;
Mother is one who always gives her best;
I love you mother because you are mine!


(N)ow, this time has come to show my respect and appreciation for all your efforts
(U)ncountable times it was tough for me without you around;
My heart still aches when I think about those moments
You deserve every bit of happiness, please stay here much longer

And all the while my heart grew wild, and I could not stay;

As once I used to watch those children stray
From out the gate, at morn or eve, by twos and threes;

For there was peace among them — though they knew not why;
The very cattle seemed as wise, as mute, as meek;
